# Netlify rewrite (proxy): a request to /api/search on this site is
# forwarded server-side to Apple's public iTunes Search API. Status
# 200 is what makes this a REWRITE rather than a redirect — the
# browser's address bar, and the origin it's actually talking to,
# never change. Since the browser only ever calls its own origin,
# there's no cross-origin request for CORS rules to apply to; the
# real cross-origin hop happens on Netlify's edge, server-to-server,
# where CORS (a browser-only mechanism) is irrelevant.
#
# Query strings pass straight through on 200 rewrites, so a client
# call to:
#   /api/search?term=daft+punk&media=music&entity=song&limit=1
# is served as:
#   https://itunes.apple.com/search?term=daft+punk&media=music&entity=song&limit=1
/api/search  https://itunes.apple.com/search  200
/api/fastsaver/*  https://api.fastsaver.io/v1/:splat  200
